{"version":"bsb","book":"job","chapter":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"heading","level":2,"text":"Bildad: Man Cannot Be Righteous"},{"kind":"paragraph","indent":0,"runs":[{"verse":1,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Then Bildad the Shuhite replied:"}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":2,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"“Dominion and awe belong to God;"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":2,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"He establishes harmony in the heights of heaven."}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":3,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"Can His troops be numbered?"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":3,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"On whom does His light not rise?"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":4,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"How then can a man be just before God?"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":4,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"How can one born of woman be pure?"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":5,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"If even the moon does not shine,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":5,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and the stars are not pure in His sight,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":6,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"how much less man, who is but a maggot,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":6,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and the son of man, who is but a worm!”"}]}]}
